## Report
Validated the finding as an information disclosure in server-side diagnostics/logging. I first reviewed the changed paths and then created a targeted Rust integration PoC at crates/server-core/tests/storage_rpc_detail_leak.rs. Source evidence: crates/server-core/src/error.rs:353-363 adds server_storage_rpc_detail(); crates/server-core/src/error.rs:617-650 formats StoreError::StorageRpc, ResourceExhausted, ShardDeleteInProgress, and nested ShardStore using raw operation/message plus node/PG/epoch details. crates/server-http/src/http/response.rs:739-746 and crates/server-http/src/http/mod.rs:660-699 attach server_detail to error diagnostics and emit it for HTTP 500. crates/observability/src/lib.rs:1465-1498 records server_detail in the flight recorder/trace event. Upstream storage RPC messages can contain raw request-derived identifiers: crates/storage/src/storage_node_server.rs:6706-6724 formats bucket.as_str() and key.as_str() into a StorageRpcErrorResponse message, and crates/storage/src/node_client.rs:4555-4574 propagates server-provided error.message into StoreError::StorageRpc. Dynamic PoC: `cargo test -p server-core --test storage_rpc_detail_leak -- --nocapture` passed and printed `SERVER_DETAIL=shard_store node_id=3 pg_id=7 cluster_epoch=1 source=(storage_rpc node_id=9 operation="GetObject" message="PayloadDecode: GetObject PG 7 does not match object secret-bucket-tenant-42/customer/pii/report.csv PG 23")`. The same test showed the redacted cause chain remained bounded (`server_error>store_error>shard_store>storage_rpc_error`) while the new `request_500_server_detail` flight-recorder event contained `secret-bucket-tenant-42`, `customer/pii/report.csv`, and PG IDs. Crash reproduction is not applicable because this is a confidentiality/logging issue rather than memory corruption; the direct PoC reliably reproduced the leak without crashing. Valgrind was attempted/checked but not installed in the container. gdb was also unavailable, so I used LLDB non-interactively: it stopped at crates/server-core/src/error.rs:359 in `ServerError::server_storage_rpc_detail`, with the backtrace leading from the PoC test at storage_rpc_detail_leak.rs:36, then continued to the leaking output.

